  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Science Applications International obligated $2.5B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Science Applications International received 828 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $3.1M. Science Applications International obligations fell 42.8% year over year. Science Applications International work is concentrated with the Department of Defense and the General Services Administration; the Department of Defense obligated $968M and the General Services Administration obligated $890M in FY2026 to date. Science Applications International sells engineering and IT services as the largest markets: Engineering Services accounted for $955M and Computer Systems Design Services accounted for $887M. Science Applications International also recorded notable work in R&D markets, with $202M in Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) and $150M in Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Biotechnology). Science Applications International totals here are fiscal year to date and represent contract obligations unless otherwise noted.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are Science Applications International's biggest federal buyers?",
        "body": "Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $968M in FY2026 to date. General Services Administration is the second largest buyer, obligating $890M. Department of Homeland Security and the Department of the Treasury follow, obligating $139M and $131M respectively."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What services and markets capture most of Science Applications International's federal spending?",
        "body": "Engineering Services is the single largest market, accounting for $955M in FY2026 to date. Computer Systems Design Services is the second largest market, accounting for $887M. Science Applications International also does substantial work in R&D markets, including $202M and $150M in the two R&D categories listed."
      }
    ]
  },
