      "q": "How much does Science Applications International make from federal contracts?",
      "a": "Science Applications International obligated $2.5B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Science Applications International received 828 awards so far and the average award size was $3.1M. Science Applications International obligations fell 42.8% year over year, reflecting a lower total compared with prior full fiscal years."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies buy from Science Applications International?",
      "a": "Department of Defense buys the most from Science Applications International, obligating $968M in FY2026 to date. General Services Administration is the next largest buyer at $890M, followed by Department of Homeland Security at $139M and Department of the Treasury at $131M."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Science Applications International sell to the government?",
